  "description": "Find the length of the longest consecutive sequence path in a binary tree where the path can be increasing or decreasing.",
  "pseudocode": "1. int maxLen = 0;\n2. int[] dfs(node) {\n3.   if (!node) return {0, 0};\n4.   int inc = 1, dec = 1;\n5.   if (node.left) {\n6.     int[] l = dfs(node.left);\n7.     if (node.val == node.left.val + 1) dec = Math.max(dec, l[1] + 1);\n8.     if (node.val == node.left.val - 1) inc = Math.max(inc, l[0] + 1);\n9.   }\n10.  if (node.right) {\n11.    int[] r = dfs(node.right);\n12.    if (node.val == node.right.val + 1) dec = Math.max(dec, r[1] + 1);\n13.    if (node.val == node.right.val - 1) inc = Math.max(inc, r[0] + 1);\n14.  }\n15.  maxLen = Math.max(maxLen, inc + dec - 1);\n16.  return {inc, dec};\n17. }",
